### 9. Data format summary (for your design docs)

| Layer | Preferred Format | Why |
|-------|------------------|-----|
| Source guidelines | PDF → extracted **plain text / Markdown** | Easy to ingest + chunk; retains headings and structure for RAG |
| Knowledge base | Chunked text (500–1500 tokens) with metadata in vector DB | Best for Nova/Claude + RAG; metadata for age group, emergency vs chronic, India vs WHO source |
| Clinical event storage | **FHIR R4 JSON** (ABDM profiles) | Directly compatible with ABDM, many Indian HIS/EMR; future proof |
| Coding inside FHIR | SNOMED‑CT, ICD‑10/11, LOINC (where relevant) | Standardised semantics; plug‑and‑play with existing health IT |

This should give you a very concrete “shopping list” for data:

- For hackathon: **E‑series, M‑series, L1, some NDMA first‑aid, plus ABDM/FHIR** are enough to prove seriousness and safety.  
- For product: gradually add ASHA/IPHS, IDSP, NPCDCS, NTEP, and richer ABDM integration.